[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello everyone! I am working on a project on Lean 4, and I was wondering if there is existing Lean 4 code providing  Kummer Congruence for Bernoulli numbers? My purpose is to construct a mathematically correct lean definition of the Kubota-Leopoldt seven-adic zeta function and its value at three. I need the standard result showing that euler corrected bernoulli values remain compatible at every level of seven-adic precision, so that they can be extended to a continuous seven adic function. Im only looking for the standard foundational infrastructure and definitions, any help would be deeply appreciated, thank you!</p>",
        "id": 623952290,
        "sender_full_name": "Yi Taifeng",
        "timestamp": 1789359755
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246273\">@Bhavik Mehta</span> has a PR about the Kummer congruence I think</p>",
        "id": 623959441,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1789362509
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My understanding is that Bhavik's recent work of 5 establishes congruences modulo p.</p>\n<p>My former student Ashvni Narayanan defined p-adic zeta functions in lean 3 following Washington's book (finding an error in it which we never got to the bottom of). But the work was never ported.</p>",
        "id": 623964737,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1789365019
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>okay thanks so much guys!</p>",
        "id": 623968929,
        "sender_full_name": "Yi Taifeng",
        "timestamp": 1789366971
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can find the kummer congruence <a href=\"https://github.com/CBirkbeck/AINTLIB/blob/main/projects%2FFltRegularBernoulli%2FBernoulliRegular%2FIrregularPrimes%2FKummerCongruenceFull.lean\">here</a> this was part of the FLT Bernoulli regular project I did with <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"130384\">@Riccardo Brasca</span></p>",
        "id": 623972835,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Birkbeck",
        "timestamp": 1789368563
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's not in mathlib, but maybe it will be in Tau Ceti soon.</p>",
        "id": 623972924,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Birkbeck",
        "timestamp": 1789368600
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think there was a Lean3 formalization project of Kubota-Leopoldt p-adic L-function (as Kevin said).</p>",
        "id": 623972967,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1789368618
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that I am already working on basically exactly this, via p-adic modular forms, see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/project-intentions/issues/21\">here</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/ANR-FALSE/PadicModForms\">here</a>.</p>",
        "id": 623973322,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1789368757
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>thank you so much everyone!</p>",
        "id": 623973649,
        "sender_full_name": "Yi Taifeng",
        "timestamp": 1789368869
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The real goal of the project is rather about overconvergent modular forms, but the first test of the definition is the p-adic zeta function. All the basic definitions are already there and I am almost sure there will be no surprises, but I am a bit busy with teaching this term.</p>",
        "id": 623973690,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1789368882
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, my point is to have a repo that is entirely human designed. I use LLMs to reorganize files, bump mathlib and other stuff like that, but all the design decisions are made by me, so it's quite slower than firing Claude at it (I am sure it can do it in less than a week).</p>",
        "id": 623974309,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1789369058
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Anyway let me know if you are interested in a collaboration!</p>",
        "id": 623975963,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1789369557
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yup sure I will dm you if interested in collaboration, thank you so much!</p>",
        "id": 623976297,
        "sender_full_name": "Yi Taifeng",
        "timestamp": 1789369641
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One thing I learnt from supervising Ashvni are that there are several things that one might mean by \"the p-adic zeta function\". Is it a function on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Z_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.975em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, a function on some <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span>-adic disc <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|s|\\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{C}_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.975em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (or a slightly bigger open disc), or a function on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span>-adic weight space <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Hom(\\Z_p^\\times,\\mathbb{C}_p^\\times)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1544em;vertical-align:-0.3831em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">o</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3831em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3831em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>? The latter is the most general case (each of the domains I mention above is strictly contained within the next one) and Ashvni did the most general case (following the later chapters of Washington).</p>",
        "id": 623992249,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1789374018
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW the issue she found in Washington's book on cyclotomic fields is the following: on p239 Theorem 12.2 he's proving that special values of p-adic L-functions are related to generalised Bernoulli numbers. He applies Lemma 7.11, which is stated and proved on pages 124-125. However 7.11 is proved within the context of Lemma 7.10 which assumes that chi is even; but the evenness hypothesis is not there in 12.2.  We never got to the bottom of this and Ashvni just added it as a hypothesis.</p>",
        "id": 623993662,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1789374408
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah I have a (WIP) PR for Kummer's congruence mod p, with the reasoning that it a) fits in the existing mathlib Bernoulli file comfortably b) doesn't need much machinery and c) is still helpful.</p>",
        "id": 624015660,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1789380202
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW, I recently added p-adic measures to mathlib (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=AbstractMeasure#doc\">docs#AbstractMeasure</a>) in the hope that it could be used as the \"natural home\" of p-adic L-functions (the definition there is an equivalent formulation of the third + most general of the alternatives in Kevin's message). As a proof of concept I used these definitions in the auto-formalization of p-adic L-functions for modular forms (<a href=\"https://prove2.me/missions/Ordinary%20p-adic%20L-functions%3A%20Mazur%E2%80%93Tate%E2%80%93Teitelbaum%20interpolation\">Prove2Me project</a>), although this is unlikely to make it into mathlib any time soon.</p>",
        "id": 624138442,
        "sender_full_name": "David Loeffler",
        "timestamp": 1789409925
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Kubota-Leopoldt.20zeta.20project/near/623992249\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>... there are several things that one might mean by \"the p-adic zeta function\". Is it a function on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Z_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.975em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, a function on some <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span>-adic disc <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|s|\\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{C}_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.975em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (or a slightly bigger open disc), or a function on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span>-adic weight space <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Hom(\\Z_p^\\times,\\mathbb{C}_p^\\times)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1544em;vertical-align:-0.3831em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">o</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3831em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3831em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If it's me, I prefer measure (or tempered distribution with possible poles in general) on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Z_p^\\times</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1544em;vertical-align:-0.3831em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">×</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3831em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>",
        "id": 624294361,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1789465416
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think most people actively researching on p-adic L-functions would prefer the measure/distribution formulation (although it is a bit less immediately intuitive for non-experts).</p>",
        "id": 624624048,
        "sender_full_name": "David Loeffler",
        "timestamp": 1789560184
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW, Kevin is telling fibs when he claims he learned about this approach to p-adic L-functions when he supervised Ashvni's thesis, because I learned it <em>from him</em> some years before!</p>",
